! mcp_bootstrap_p233.strap -- MCP printed page 233: the Input Program's
! scan/byte section (V COMX .. LVI,V T2,V BF1), lines 1-56.
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.240, read at 400 dpi, 900 dpi for
! doubtful glyphs.  Header, READ: "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP
! CARD ID CA000892  DIST. OF 3/01  3/01  PAGE NUMBER 233"; the heading
! row's LOCATION field is 225120, line 1's word.
!
! THE PAGE.  56 lines, 55 located, contiguous from 225120.00 to
! 225160.00 (a half word; next location 225160.40).  Line 32 is a
! comment card with no location (remark "-009").  The volume OCR puts
! the row before this page (p.232) at 225117.40, so line 1 joins it.
! Remarks are sequence numbers -0868 .. -0915, printed at varying
! columns; lines 5 and 32 print short ones, "-010" and "-009" (round
! glyphs read 0 in a numeric field).  Asterisks after the LOCATION on
! lines 12, 30, 51.
!
! LABEL SPELLINGS SETTLED BY OTHER THAN PLAIN INK:
!   * line 23 "V CFFLB" = VOFFLB, line 26 "V CFFX" = VOFFX, line 42
!     "V CNLIB" = VONLIB: worn O.  Landed p.215 references VOFFLB
!     (225136.0) and VONLIB (225151.0) -- exactly these LOCATIONs;
!     line 24 BZXVZ,V OFFX prints 225140.31 = line 26's location.
!   * line 2 "V COMX": the second glyph is ambiguous (O/D) at 900 dpi;
!     written VCOMX after V COM (line 3, printed "V CCM", landed decks
!     spell VCOM).  Nothing on this page references it -- rests on ink.
!   * line 5 "VCBR" (printed with no space): line 1 LVNI,V T5,V CBR
!     prints 225122.23 = this row's 225122.00 + J 9.
!   * line 23 "V PCB+1." = VPDB: at 900 dpi the third glyph has a
!     straight left stem (D, worn); volume OCR of its XW card reads
!     "V PD XW,V PCB" at 225427 with value 225435.00.
!   * line 27 "BR,C" is BR,0: binary 000000.14 00, address 0.
!   * hex bytes printed with an open round written 0 ("C0", "C9" ...),
!     octal fields "CCCCCC.CC" are 0.
!   * line 36 "V CP": the defining card (not landed) reads, in the
!     volume OCR, "V CP SYN(BU,1),3." at a later page.
!
! LENGTH 32 FROM AN INSTRUCTION'S NAME.  L/ST with no dds print 040000.20
! when the operand names a half-word instruction: "instruction-naming
! symbols are given field lengths equal to the lengths of the particular
! instructions named (either 32 or 64) ... byte size 8" (C22-6531
! printed p.10), so those stand-in SYNs carry (BU,32,8).
!
! CARD SERIALS.  Right-hand serials run ?A000892 .. ?A000939 (prefix
! glyph D-shaped, as in the header's CA000892).  Pairs share a serial:
! lines 2/3 (893), 7/8 (897), 26/27 (915), 28/29 (916), 33/34 (920),
! 37/38 (923), 42/43 (927), 45/46 (929).  Line 32 (the comment card)
! carries 919.  No serial is skipped.

